            <ArticleTitle>Acute haemorrhagic pancreatitis - A case of sudden death.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jflm.2008.08.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sudden death in young individuals is relatively uncommon and acute haemorrhagic pancreatitis as a cause of sudden and unexpected death is a rare phenomenon. A case of sudden death due to acute haemorrhagic pancreatitis is reported in a young doctor who ignored the radiating pain of acute pancreatitis for gastritis, and resorted to self-medication. The condition was discovered only at autopsy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
